
LOCK(1)             UNIX Programmer's Manual              LOCK(1)

NAME
     lock - reserve a terminal

SYNOPSIS
     lock

DESCRIPTION
     _L_o_c_k requests a password from the user, then prints "LOCKED"
     on the terminal and refuses to relinquish the terminal until
     the password is repeated.  If the user forgets the password,
     he has no other recourse but to login elsewhere and kill the
     lock process.

AUTHOR
     Kurt Shoens

BUGS
     Should timeout after 15 minutes.

